> API and interpretation

Empty RHS represents epsilon; empty symbol strings and reserved $/__START__
symbols are invalid grammar symbols. A defined start rule is required.
Constructed state/table snapshots own copies. Parsing a conflicted grammar
throws, unknown terminals reject, and an embedded end marker rejects rather than
allowing an early prefix accept. The legacy depth trace remains initial depth
plus actual shift/reduce depths, empty on rejection. No real dataset is needed
for this grammar mechanism.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

